{
  // ── The SHARED compiler options (MOTIR-4293) ────────────────────────────────
  //
  // Moved verbatim out of `tsconfig.json`, which used to be the repository's ONE
  // program: `include: ["**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx", …]` over app code, tests, scripts
  // and the generated Prisma client together. Checker memory is proportional to
  // the program, so tests, scripts and product code each paid for the others'
  // types — 4.19 GB against node 22's ~4.1 GB default old-space, and 5.08 GB with
  // one more Prisma model on top (MOTIR-3878). Two heap bumps in one repository
  // (the `build` job at MOTIR-1789, this one at MOTIR-3878) is the tree saying its
  // SHAPE is wrong, not its heap.
  //
  // ⚠️ "THE PROGRAM" MEANS EVERY FILE THE CHECKER LOADS, DECLARATIONS INCLUDED —
  // NOT THE FILES YOU WROTE (MOTIR-4422). The sentence above is measured and
  // correct; what it does not say, and what three documents in this repository
  // went on to assume, is which files it is counting. Seven runs of
  // `assert-typecheck-headroom.mjs` over one unchanged tree, node 22, default heap
  // 4.05 GB:
  //
  //   project                       own bodies   files in program      used
  //   baseline probe                         1                248   0.14 GB
  //   tsconfig.e2e.json                    185                934   0.71 GB
  //   tsconfig.scripts.json                116               2026   1.64 GB
  //   tsconfig.app.json                      —               5530   2.25 GB
  //   tsconfig.tests.json                 1682               7013   3.35 GB
  //
  // Least squares through the origin over those: **0.48 MB per file in the
  // program**, and the fixed cost of a project that imports nothing of ours is
  // **0.14 GB (3.4%)** — measured directly, by a project with the tests project's
  // own options and references and ONE test body
  // (`assert-typecheck-headroom.mjs --baseline`).
  //
  // Two consequences, and the second is the one that has cost cards:
  //
  //   1. **There is no floor a project pays for REFERENCING another.**
  //      Declarations load on demand: `tsconfig.e2e.json` references this same app
  //      project, has MORE bodies than `tsconfig.scripts.json`, and costs less than
  //      half as much. A project's cost is its bodies PLUS the declaration closure
  //      those bodies import — its own closure, not a shared surcharge.
  //   2. **So what a project BOUNDARY buys is whatever it removes from the
  //      PROGRAM** — the bodies it moves, plus only those declarations that nothing
  //      left behind still imports. A line drawn where the two halves import the
  //      same `lib/` surface moves bodies and keeps declarations, and returns
  //      little. Measured: splitting `tests/components/**` (298 of 1682 bodies, the
  //      largest single subdirectory) takes the ceiling from 7013 files / 82.8% to
  //      6212 files / 77.3% — 801 files, 5.5 points.
  //
  // **Price a boundary before you draw it, in one command**: the `files` column
  // `assert-typecheck-headroom.mjs` already prints IS the variable, so a candidate
  // config's file count answers what it would cost. Do not estimate a split from a
  // count of test files.
  //
  // Nothing extends this file for its own sake. It exists so the four real
  // projects — `tsconfig.json` (Next's product program), `tsconfig.tests.json`,
  // `tsconfig.scripts.json` and the composite `tsconfig.app.json` layered on the
  // first — state one set of options once. `tsconfig.solution.json` composes them.
  //
  // ⚠️ `paths` LIVES HERE, and that is load-bearing: `@/*` maps to `./*` relative
  // to the file that DECLARES it, so every project resolves `@/lib/x` to the same
  // place. Under `tsc -b` a tests-project import of `@/lib/x` then redirects to
  // the app project's emitted `.tsout/app/lib/x.d.ts` rather than re-checking the
  // source — which is the whole point of the split.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2017",
    "lib": ["dom", "dom.iterable", "esnext"],
    "allowJs": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "strict": true,
    "noImplicitAny": true,
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true,
    "noImplicitOverride": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "module": "esnext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "incremental": true,
    "plugins": [
      {
        "name": "next"
      }
    ],
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./*"]
    }
  }
}
